+    "caa8_key_findings_brief": "Deviations improved out-of-sample prediction for overall psychopathology, positive psychosis, and fear versus raw volume. Regional deviations in vmPFC, inferior temporal, and daCC correlated more with overall psychopathology than specific dimensions. Case–control deviation effects overlapped and were reduced after controlling for overall psychopathology.",
+    "caa9_key_findings_detailed": "Across multiple scoring metrics (correlation, neg[RMSE], neg[MAE]), deviations yielded comparable or superior predictive performance to raw cortical volume, with significant gains for overall psychopathology and positive psychosis (and fear for MAE). No dimension showed raw volume outperforming deviations when deviations were non-significant. Regionally, deviations in vmPFC/mOFC, inferior temporal, and daCC related more strongly to overall psychopathology than dimension-specific scores. In case–control analyses (depression, ADHD), spatially overlapping deviation effects diminished when controlling for overall psychopathology, supporting shared disorder-general components.",
